      "settlement": "Faeloryth",
      "settlementKey": "gruddirynn:Faeloryth",
      "description": "Clem Softspade is a good-natured Grudgel test citizen whose eagerness to help makes him painfully easy for ambitious overseers to exploit. At the Faeloryth Watch Office, he volunteers for bunker trials, safety demonstrations, comfort experiments, and other Regent Lattice projects that everyone insists are perfectly harmless right up until they are not. Clem is awkward, trusting, and much smarter emotionally than his handlers realize, especially when he begins noticing which tests make people less kind.",
      "settlementAndAncestryTexture": "Faeloryth is a Town in Gruddirynn, under Aristocracy, with severe danger, Beach and reefs with water, Ocean Surface floating settlement, Beach and grass with water terrain. Local records favor Neutral, Lawful, Cooperative, Honorable civic habits; common communities include Human, Halfling — Lightfoot Halfling, Elf — Sea Elf, Tortle, Genasi — Water Genasi. Grudgel reads through the Grudgel entry of the race compendium, within Primitive, Tribal, and Wilderness Humanoids, marked by Asethyr. Hardy mountain-forged tribal humanoids shaped by long memory and inherited vendettas. They are stoic, resilient, and slow to forgive but fiercely loyal. Table cues: Battlefield Control, Centered, Darkvision, Powerful Build; starting tendency Neutral - Chaotic - Neutral - Honorable.",
      "rumors": [
        "Clem Softspade knows why an ichor ledger changed hands last Anubaday.",
        "Clem Softspade has a contact in Virethéa who will deny everything."
      ],
      "plotHooks": [
